# Visualization

Use this rule when adding a plot, a paper figure, or a notebook that exports one.

Plotly is for exploration. matplotlib or seaborn is for the paper. Call `apply_matplotlib_style`. Use the Okabe–Ito cycle from `valmorph.viz.theme`. Do not introduce a second palette.

Every exported paper figure has a provenance JSON from `write_provenance`: git commit, config hash, seeds, ledger version, ledger content hashes, devices. The notebook cell that writes the figure is the one that writes the manifest.

Title synthetic figures with the prefix `SYNTHETIC`. Do not pass them to `assert_citable`.

Required visual analyses, once the data exist: edit timeline, neuron lineage tree, animated topology, diagnostic heatmap, forgetting matrix, Level 1 curve, Level 2 curve. Each one is a function in `src/valmorph/viz` plus a thin notebook cell.

A finding that a figure supports is also a `findings` row with `evidence_ref` pointing at the manifest.
